    "durationMs": 194879,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. What I built and confirmed:\n\n**Implementation** (Rails 8.0.2 API-only, Ruby 3.4.3, PostgreSQL via `DATABASE_URL`):\n- `app/models/link.rb` — URL validation (absolute http/https with host) and code format (`\\A[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}\\z`), uniqueness on `code`\n- `app/controllers/links_controller.rb` — create (auto/custom code, duplicate → 409), show (404 JSON), index (ascending by id, `{\"items\", \"total\"}`), plus malformed-JSON → 422 and a raw-body fallback for requests without a Content-Type header\n- `app/controllers/redirects_controller.rb` — 302 with exact stored URL in `Location`, atomic SQL-level click increment\n- `config/database.yml` reads credentials only from `DATABASE_URL`; host allowlisting disabled so any hostname works\n\n**Verified via `sh start.sh`** (which runs `db:prepare` then serves foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`):\n- All status codes and JSON shapes match the spec (201/409/422/404/302/200), including code-length boundaries (20 ok, 21 rejected), ftp/relative/hostless URLs rejected, and URL returned unchanged (query strings, ports, `&`)\n- Clicks increment exactly once per redirect and survive restarts; data survives restarts\n- Dropped the database entirely and rebooted via `start.sh` — it recreated, migrated, and served correctly (role has CREATEDB)\n- Left the database empty, log truncated, and port 8000 free for the automated test suite\n\nREADME includes a \"Starting the server\" section explaining `sh start.sh` and the `DATABASE_URL` requirement."
